  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>runstest</keyword>
  <short_description>Runs test for randomness.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>h = runstest(x)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = runstest(x, v)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = runstest(x, 'ud')</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = runstest(..., Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[h, p, stats] = runstest(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>runstest</b> tests whether values in a vector appear in random order. The default test counts runs above and below the mean of <b>x</b>. A scalar <b>v</b> can be supplied as a reference value. The <b>ud</b> mode counts runs up and down.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>Method</b>, and <b>Tail</b>. <b>NaN</b> values and values exactly equal to the reference are omitted.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [1 2 3 4 5 0 -1 -2];
[h, p, stats] = runstest(x)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
